{
  "name": "266. Agent Gateway push configurations are tenant-scoped and stream replies fail closed (a2a-push-tenancy) [SERIAL]",
  "description": "TXE-5477 (PR5 preservation group 3a). The gateway stores each client's push callback itself and proxies the rest to the upstream agent; the fixture agent is tests/e2e/api/runners/a2a-push-fixture.mjs on 127.0.0.1:18091 (override with the a2aPushFixtureUrl variable), started by test-provider-harness.sh. Pins: a push configuration belongs to the tenant that registered it (another tenant naming the same task and config ID cannot replace, read, list or delete it; a tenantless request is the empty tenant, not a wildcard); a plain JSON reply to SendStreamingMessage is reframed as one SSE event, while a malformed or oversized one surfaces as an error event instead of an empty or truncated successful stream; a registration created with enabled false reads back disabled. The folder sets a2a_external_client_url for its own rows (reading the current client config first, since PUT /api/config validates the whole object) and clears it at the end, so folder 233's missing-URL rows keep their meaning in a full run. Red on main ff00d1500 at 266.5 (the callback is replaced), 266.6-266.12 (cross-tenant reads, lists and delete), 266.16-266.17 (empty stream) and 266.19 (enabled true); green on this change.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "266.1 a2a push tenancy: set a2a_external_client_url so the gateway can mint push callbacks",
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"client_config\": {{a2aClientConfig}}}"
        },
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/config"
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// One fixture agent per run; the registration is deleted at the end of the folder.",
              "if (!pm.variables.get('a2aPushAgent')) { pm.variables.set('a2aPushAgent', 'a2a-push-fixture-' + Date.now()); }",
              "pm.variables.set('a2aFixtureBase', pm.variables.get('a2aPushFixtureUrl') || 'http://127.0.0.1:18091');",
              "// PUT /api/config validates the whole client config, so read the current one and change only the URL.",
              "var headers = { 'Accept': 'application/json' };",
              "var setupToken = pm.variables.get('setupToken');",
              "if (setupToken) { headers['X-Bifrost-Setup-Token'] = setupToken; }",
              "pm.sendRequest({ url: pm.variables.get('baseUrl') + '/api/config', method: 'GET', header: headers }, function (err, res) {",
              "  if (err) { throw err; }",
              "  if (res.code !== 200) { throw new Error('GET /api/config returned ' + res.code + ': ' + res.text()); }",
              "  var clientConfig = res.json().client_config || {};",
              "  // The server reports log_retention_days 0 by default but rejects that on write (as set-raw-override-config.mjs notes).",
              "  if (!(clientConfig.log_retention_days >= 1)) { clientConfig.log_retention_days = 1; }",
              "  clientConfig.a2a_external_client_url = pm.variables.get('baseUrl');",
              "  pm.variables.set('a2aClientConfig', JSON.stringify(clientConfig));",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () { pm.expect(pm.response.code, pm.response.text()).to.equal(200); });"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
